ber each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids, the most of any pair. In 2025, September to October ran 33% of normal on the middle of the grids and October to November ran 48%. This year so far, May to June came in at 191% of normal in 2026, after March to April sat at 42% in 2026. Every grid had its driest year in 1954.</p>"}
